WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.205
Recruiters and clients often send me a short coding test before the first call. I want the job, so I open it.

2
00:00:10.205 --> 00:00:19.682
Binance says its $6.3 billion hack started the same way: an engineer ran a recruiter's coding test on his work laptop.

3
00:00:19.682 --> 00:00:29.773
A test like that, opened in VS Code on my own account. It asks if I trust the authors. Most of us click yes.

4
00:00:29.773 --> 00:00:34.886
Then it asks if the folder's tasks can run. I allow it.

5
00:00:34.886 --> 00:00:40.224
Something starts by itself. This one is harmless, and the secrets are fake.

6
00:00:40.224 --> 00:00:46.793
In seconds it finds an SSH key, cloud logins, three crypto wallets and saved browser passwords.

7
00:00:46.793 --> 00:00:51.659
13 secrets, all in reach. A real one wouldn't just look.

8
00:00:51.659 --> 00:01:00.773
The safe answer is a virtual machine. But setting one up takes an evening, and for a one-hour test, most people skip it.

9
00:01:00.773 --> 00:01:11.114
So I built Spare Room. It creates a spare room: a second Windows account with nothing in it. On my laptop, that took 30 seconds.

10
00:01:11.114 --> 00:01:14.523
Now I'm signed in to the spare room.

11
00:01:14.523 --> 00:01:24.864
Can I still do the test here? Node, npm and Git are ready. Python and VS Code need one install, for all users.

12
00:01:24.864 --> 00:01:31.227
Now the same check, against the same 13 secrets. Blocked. All 13.

13
00:01:31.227 --> 00:01:38.859
Spare Room also checks from the inside. All 12 secret locations in my account are out of reach.

14
00:01:38.859 --> 00:01:48.114
One .env sits in a shared folder every account can read. Spare Room points it out, so I can move it.

15
00:01:48.114 --> 00:01:51.543
You shouldn't have to trust a security tool blindly.

16
00:01:51.543 --> 00:01:57.227
Spare Room works with the Wi-Fi off, and it never reads a secret's value.

17
00:01:57.227 --> 00:02:03.132
It's weaker than a virtual machine. It also takes 30 seconds instead of an evening.

18
00:02:03.132 --> 00:02:09.386
13 reachable, then 0. Before you run a stranger's code, give it a spare room.
